  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"1.8.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: libpisp\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/raspberrypi/libpisp/archive/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 753a31b907258e05070215be515a4051bb76bcbad3d74293d779cbb5f59446d4\n  patches:\n    - dma-heap.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip: not linux\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - meson\n    - ninja\n    - pkg-config\n  host:\n    - nlohmann_json\n  run:\n    # libpisp.pc lists nlohmann_json in Requires.private, so pkg-config/meson\n    # lookups of libpisp fail without it (header-only, so this is cheap).\n    - nlohmann_json\n  run_exports:\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage('libpisp', upper_bound='x.x') }}\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      lib:\n        - pisp\n      include:\n        - libpisp/backend/backend.hpp\n        - libpisp/frontend/frontend.hpp\n      files:\n        - lib/pkgconfig/libpisp.pc\n        - lib/libpisp/backend/backend_default_config.json\n        - share/libpisp/backend_default_config.json\n  - script:\n      - pkg-config --exists --print-errors libpisp\n      - test \"$(pkg-config --modversion libpisp)\" = \"${{ version }}\"\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - pkg-config\n\nabout:\n  summary: Library for interfacing with the Raspberry Pi PISP\n  license: BSD-2-Clause AND GPL-2.0-only WITH Linux-syscall-note\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - LICENSES/\n  homepage: https://github.com/raspberrypi/libpisp\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - carlodri\n",
